# Entry Main: one call, one execution (the book #structural-call; step 21.7 K3). The body of C counts its runs in node\count,
# a field of D (node in C is D), and returns 6: it is called in a value context (`D\C() + 1`, r 7) and as a statement,
# whose result is discarded. D\count 2 after two calls: neither the body nor the result is evaluated twice.
int: r 0
D:
    int: count 0
    return: int
    C:
        node\count := node\count + 1
        return: 6
---
Main:
    node\r := D\C() + 1
    D\C()
